  SKILL.md is derived from its SKILL.md, with changes: the skill was
  renamed, a refutation pass per finding, a diff mode, tool evidence,
  variant analysis, exclusion rules and new guides were added, and the
  output format was extended. The verbatim copies are listed in UPSTREAM.

  Five copies were changed.
  2026-10-09: references/injection.md line 235. Its
  pattern `grep -rn "\\.query\\(.*\\+"` fails in GNU grep ("Unmatched ( or \("),
  because \( opens a group in a basic regular expression; it now reads
  `grep -rn '\.query(.*+'`.
  2026-10-10: languages/python.md line 150. The example
  `app.secret_key = '<a 9-letter word>'` reads as a credential to secret
  masking tools (a label, then a quoted value of 8 or more characters), and a
  guard built on them refused to print the whole guide; the literal is now
  `'dev'`, which still shows a hard-coded key.
  2026-10-10: four more examples that masking tools read as credentials,
  for the same reason. references/injection.md line 185: the LDAP filter is
  built with String.format instead of `"…(userPassword=" + safePassword +
  "))"`, which read as a quoted value after a label. references/ssrf.md lines
  305-306: the timeouts are named constants instead of literals, because a
  lone `obj.setX(5000);` line read as a password. references/supply-chain.md
  line 149: the example key value is `<hard-coded key>`.
  references/misconfiguration.md lines 150, 156 and 160: the default
  passwords are shorter well-known ones (`admin`, `toor`), still defaults.

